    turnFlow: "1. Players take turns. Each turn begins with drawing 1 card from the stock.\n2. You can play any card from your hand onto a pile if it is one rank lower and a different color (e.g., a Red 7 onto a Black 8).\n3. You can move an entire pile onto another pile if the bottom card of the first fits on the top card of the second.\n4. **Kings**: If you have a King, it *must* be played into one of the empty 'Corner' slots (diagonals of the cross). Once there, it forms a new foundation pile.\n5. Empty Slots: If one of the original 4 foundation slots becomes empty, you can place any card (or sequence) there.",
